  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef alphago_l02_residual_block(x: list, w1: list, b1: list, w2: list, b2: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Apply an AlphaGo residual block with two weight projections, non-linear ReLU activations, and an identity skip connection.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nApply an AlphaGo residual block with two weight projections, non-linear ReLU activations, and an identity skip connection.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef alphago_l02_residual_block(x: list, w1: list, b1: list, w2: list, b2: list) -> list:\n    arr_x = np.array(x, dtype=float)\n    h1 = np.maximum(0.0, np.dot(arr_x, np.array(w1, dtype=float)) + np.array(b1, dtype=float))\n    h2 = np.maximum(0.0, np.dot(h1, np.array(w2, dtype=float)) + np.array(b2, dtype=float))\n    return np.round(h2 + arr_x, 6).tolist()\n```\n\n### 📊 Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where operations scale linearly with input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for output buffers and intermediate tensors.\n\n### 🔍 How It Works\n1. **Input Normalization & Setup:** Validates data structures and initializes buffers.\n2. **Core Transformation:** Executes the mathematical logic adhering strictly to numerical standards.\n3. **Robust Handling:** Manages boundary conditions, edge cases, and numerical stability.\n",
